# acl1 — ACL users
#
# Learn: an ACL rule line is: user <name> on|off >password ~keypattern
# &channelpattern +@category -@category +command -command. Start from
# nothing (-@all, no ~ pattern) and add only what's needed; +@read,
# +@write, +@list, +@hash... are command categories (ACL CAT lists them).
#
# Task: give each app only what it needs:
#   reporter (password report-pass): read-only commands, and only on
#            keys matching report:*
#   worker   (password worker-pass): list commands only, on queue:*
# Leave the default user as it is: the check needs it.
#
# ACL files have no comment syntax, so the check drops the lines
# starting with # before loading this file.
#

user default on nopass ~* &* +@all
user reporter on >report-pass ~* +@all
user worker on >worker-pass ~* +@all
